<title>LITHUANIA: CURRENCY FIXINGS FOR MARCH 21.</title>
<headline>CURRENCY FIXINGS FOR MARCH 21.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Lithuania set the following currency fixings for Friday, March 21 on Thursday. The litas is pegged to the U.S. dollar at a rate of four to one.</p>
<p>		   21.03.97	  20.03.97     </p>
<p>    USD	     4.0000	 4.000</p>
<p>    GBP	     6.3854	 6.3716	 </p>
<p>    DEM	     2.3851	 2.3790	 </p>
<p>    ECU	     4.6130	 4.6046	 </p>
<p>    100JPY	  3.2626	 3.2486	 </p>
<p>    SEK	     0.5211	 0.5202	 </p>
<p>    FIM	     0.7922	 0.7908	 </p>
<p>    EKK	     0.2981	 0.2973	 </p>
<p>    LAT	     6.9043	 6.8853	 </p>
<p>    1000RUR	 0.6992	 0.6997	 </p>
<p>    PLN	     1.3019	 1.3029</p>
<p>--Ed Stoddard, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
